{
    "background_story": "Armani, a vibrant blue-and-yellow macaw, was named after the legendary Aztec emperor Montezuma. His owner, a historian, was fascinated by the ancient civilization and hoped that Armani would embody the same grandeur and majesty. As it turned out, Armani lived up to his namesake's reputation. He was a regal bird with a commanding presence, known for his striking plumage and impressive wingspan. Armani's intelligence and curiosity rivaled that of his namesake, who was said to possess great wisdom and strategic thinking. With a vocabulary of over 100 words, Armani would often squawk '\u00a1Viva Montezuma!' whenever he sensed excitement or celebration. His owner believed that Armani's spirit was a reincarnation of the great emperor's, and the parrot's antics and quirks only reinforced this notion.",
